commit 65df57edcb6e754449060feac9bffa52de669262
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 4 18:02:14 2026 +0000

    Add Sound, Play words automatically and Show IPA settings
    
    The owner asked for sound on every card, with autoplay chosen in
    Settings, a global sound switch that greys the speakers out, and the IPA
    for every word. This adds the settings those need, stored like the
    others: sound (on), playing words automatically (off), Show IPA (on),
    and a count of speaker taps for the long-press hint.
    
    Sound off is as if the phone had no voice for any language: nothing is
    spoken, and listening is left out of lessons, reviews, Today's counts
    and number practice, through a new AppState.canSpeak. hasVoice and
    voiceStatus stay the phone's own, so Voices and Settings still show the
    real voices, and a deck's Listening row says sound is off, with Turn on.
    
    The interface strings for the speaker and the IPA line come in here too,
    with the settings that name them.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Hxozk8Tp6QhwCiBraJpHGM

